From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilia Alshanetsky <ilia@ilia.ws>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Reject unbalanced and overly deep type names

TypeParser::Parse() called top() and pop() on its element stack for every
closing parenthesis and comma, so a type name with a surplus ')' or a
top-level ',' read from an empty std::stack. It also had no nesting limit,
and the column factory and TypeAst destruction recurse once per level, so a
type name nested 100000 levels deep exhausted the native stack. The parser
now rejects a ')' or ',' that has no open parenthesis and any type nested
deeper than TypeParser::kMaxNestingDepth (512) levels. Current servers
reject column types nested deeper than 499 levels, and 512 levels keep the
recursive paths to about 250 KiB of stack at -O2.
---
 clickhouse/types/type_parser.cpp | 6 ++++++
 clickhouse/types/type_parser.h   | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/clickhouse/types/type_parser.cpp
+++ b/clickhouse/types/type_parser.cpp
@@ -194,16 +194,22 @@
                 type_->value_string = std::string(token.value);
                 break;
             case Token::LPar:
+                if (open_elements_.size() > kMaxNestingDepth)
+                    return false;
                 type_->elements.emplace_back(TypeAst());
                 open_elements_.push(type_);
                 type_ = &type_->elements.back();
                 break;
             case Token::RPar:
+                if (open_elements_.size() < 2)
+                    return false;
                 type_ = open_elements_.top();
                 open_elements_.pop();
                 break;
             case Token::Assign:
             case Token::Comma:
+                if (open_elements_.size() < 2)
+                    return false;
                 type_ = open_elements_.top();
                 open_elements_.pop();
                 type_->elements.emplace_back(TypeAst());
--- a/clickhouse/types/type_parser.h
+++ b/clickhouse/types/type_parser.h
@@ -71,6 +71,11 @@
     };
 
 public:
+    // Current servers reject column types nested deeper than 499 levels. The
+    // column factory and TypeAst destruction recurse once per level, so the
+    // limit also bounds their stack use.
+    static constexpr size_t kMaxNestingDepth = 512;
+
     explicit TypeParser(const StringView& name);
     ~TypeParser();
 
